                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> I don't have a problem with these constants.\n\nDo you think they make the code better?  This isn't enabling some feature for the submitter...its just a refactor so there should be some benefit.  What is it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Something on my todo list has actually been to remove the pdi dependency from the mapper."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> Something on my todo list has actually been to remove the pdi dependency from the mapper.\n\nElaborating...I sort of understand the desire in other OpenBMC projects.  But the mapper follows the conventions of typical dbus application programming where the service schema is defined and discovered by the well known service name.  It will never make dbus calls to other openbmc services and thus the whole 'check the api at build time' is not applicable."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Something on my todo list has actually been to remove the pdi dependency from the mapper.\n\nTo what end? Does it meaningfully improve the build time?\n\nIf the PDI headers introduce too much overhead then that's something we can try to improve. Let me know if there is an issue there.\n\nOr are you more concerned with reducing the amount of dependencies?\n\n> It will never make dbus calls to other openbmc services and thus the whole 'check the api at build time' is not applicable.\n\nMapper depends on the `xyz.openbmc_project.Association.Definitions` interface, which is defined in PDI. So we have a dependency on that definition.\n\nWe can manually copy-paste the information about the interface into the application or simply use the generated header. Using the generated header is more convenient IMO.\n\nMapper also has a dependency on the `xyz.openbmc_project.Association` interface which it must create. Which is also defined in the PDI. So there is also a dependency there."
                }
            ],
